                  {
                    "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Validate the clone source before dropping the target**\n\nWhen `--mode clone --force` uses a source predating migration 146, this check runs only after the destination has been dropped, recreated, restored, and modified by `_post_clone_cleanup`; the advertised `RuntimeError` therefore destroys the previous slot and leaves an unusable replacement without `story_identity`. Check the source for this table before disposing or dropping the target so this known incompatibility fails before any destructive operation.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L49-L50](https://github.com/pythagorakase/nexus/blob/7ac530a11d7b66d9b23bd5171e362ae13958d1b4/AGENTS.md#L49-L50)\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
                    "url": "https://github.com/pythagorakase/nexus/pull/1117#discussion_r4214866845",
                    "originalCommit": {
                      "oid": "7ac530a11d7b66d9b23bd5171e362ae13958d1b4"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "PRRT_kwDOOBe0Mc6qM9Cs",
              "isResolved": true,
              "isOutdated": false,
              "comments": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preflight every database before starting the backfill**\n\nWhen `--all` encounters a later target without migration 146, or later discovers that a fork parent has a non-backfill identity, earlier targets have already committed new UUIDs in separate transactions before the command raises. This contradicts the function's stated pre-write refusal contract and leaves a partially backfilled fleet; inspect every target and fork parent, including tables, identities, origins, and existing lineage, before the first insert.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L49-L50](https://github.com/pythagorakase/nexus/blob/7ac530a11d7b66d9b23bd5171e362ae13958d1b4/AGENTS.md#L49-L50)\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
                    "url": "https://github.com/pythagorakase/nexus/pull/1117#discussion_r4214866858",
                    "originalCommit": {
                      "oid": "7ac530a11d7b66d9b23bd5171e362ae13958d1b4"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "PRRT_kwDOOBe0Mc6qM9C2",
              "isResolved": true,
              "isOutdated": true,
              "comments": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Update the stamped-template initialization fixture**\n\nThis unconditional write breaks the existing PostgreSQL cases `test_fresh_database_is_baseline_stamped[fresh]` and `[desktop-reset]`: their `template_db` fixture deliberately provides a minimal schema with every migration stamped, so migration 146 is not replayed and `replace_story_identity` raises `UndefinedTable`. The commit's verification records both failures; add the new identity schema to that fixture so the repository's established initialization suite remains green.\n\nAGENTS.md reference: [AGENTS.md:L55-L56](https://github.com/pythagorakase/nexus/blob/7ac530a11d7b66d9b23bd5171e362ae13958d1b4/AGENTS.md#L55-L56)\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
