                  {
                    "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Redact user-controlled mapping keys from validation locations**\n\nWhen malformed configuration places a secret-shaped string in a valid mapping key\u2014for example, a provider key under `[global.model.api_models]` with an invalid nested field\u2014Pydantic includes that key in the middle of `error[\"loc\"]`. This code redacts only the final component for `extra_forbidden`, while `_safe_token` preserves values such as `sk-...`, so the supposedly sanitized receipt can write the secret verbatim. Redact every user-controlled mapping-key component or retain only allowlisted schema field names.\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
                    "url": "https://github.com/pythagorakase/nexus/pull/1118#discussion_r4214902511",
                    "originalCommit": {
                      "oid": "e7f7a29d0e099173f44dcf8a0f87ac45a14c446c"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "PRRT_kwDOOBe0Mc6qNCRf",
              "isResolved": false,
              "isOutdated": true,
              "comments": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Deduplicate coincident home and fallback receipt roots**\n\nWhen `NEXUS_HOME` is the user's home directory, both roots resolve to `$HOME/.nexus/receipts`. Adding the same directory under two labels makes `_read_receipts` scan every file twice, doubling each group's count and falsely reporting both `home` and `fallback`; avoid adding the fallback root when it resolves to the home root.\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
                    "url": "https://github.com/pythagorakase/nexus/pull/1118#discussion_r4214902524",
                    "originalCommit": {
                      "oid": "e7f7a29d0e099173f44dcf8a0f87ac45a14c446c"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "PRRT_kwDOOBe0Mc6qNCRl",
              "isResolved": false,
              "isOutdated": true,
              "comments": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Translate receipt decoding failures into read errors**\n\nIf a receipt file contains invalid UTF-8\u2014possible when `_append` leaves a short write ending midway through a Unicode path\u2014decoding fails during stream iteration before `model_validate_json` enters its exception handler. The resulting `UnicodeDecodeError` bypasses `ReceiptReadError`, so `nexus receipts` emits a traceback rather than its documented `domain_failure`; catch decoding and file-read errors and wrap them with the receipt path and line context.\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
                    "url": "https://github.com/pythagorakase/nexus/pull/1118#discussion_r4214902533",
                    "originalCommit": {
                      "oid": "e7f7a29d0e099173f44dcf8a0f87ac45a14c446c"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
